{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>For our inheritance has come to us</b> – We have already received it on the eastern side; this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 32:19). But it is not fitting that they should speak thus before Moses, saying 'we have already received it,' for it is not in their hands; rather, the matter depends on his will, and they did not receive it until he gives it to them. But this is what they said: 'For you shall not give us an inheritance with them' — excluding their portion in the good land that belongs to them — 'for the inheritance suited to us has come to us,' namely, the land of livestock, and we have livestock more than the other tribes. And this is the way of request, not the way of contention. Alternatively, they said: 'For we shall not take an inheritance with them,' for even if you do not wish to give us the land now, we will cross over with them, we and all that is ours; but we shall not take an inheritance with them, for we will return to this land, which is the inheritance suited to us, which we desire, and which the rest of the tribes do not desire at all.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The verb תַנְחִילֵנוּ in the verse is rendered in the causative ('you shall not give/cause us to inherit'), following the regular Hebrew form, rather than the reflexive 'we shall inherit.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:09:58.878696920Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}